nd-up), crystallising just over \u00a31m of losses which were fully provided for.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management (Q4) Outturn","as_of_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22447/Treasury Management Q4 Outturn.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-07","signals":[{"code":"low-liquidity","headline":"Treasury investments fell \u00a321.1m in one year to \u00a316.2m at 31 March 2026, against \u00a376.2m debt and a \u00a3103.5m CFR","why":"Internal-borrowing headroom is nearly spent, so further capital spend or a cash shock pushes Charnwood into external borrowing at 5-6% PWLB rates roughly 2 points above its 3.38% portfolio average."},{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Council states new long-term borrowing 'will be necessary' for unfinanced capital expenditure and maturing debt, with financing proposals in a Capital Plan update in autumn 2026 (HRA added \u00a34.97m unfinanced capex in 2025/26)","why":"A flagged pipeline of new borrowing demand arriving when PWLB rates are at their most expensive in the report's own charts."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3103,525k total (General Fund \u00a322,361k, HRA \u00a381,164k)","as_at":"31/03/2026","page":6},{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a376,190k, all HRA, average rate 3.38%, average life 12.6 years (was \u00a378,190k a year earlier)","as_at":"31/03/26","page":8},{"name":"debt repaid in year","value":"\u00a32m PWLB/HRA loan repaid in October; no new borrowing undertaken during the year","as_at":"2025/26","page":12},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a316,210k, down from \u00a337,350k at 31/03/25; total net debt swung from -\u00a314,357k (net investor) to +\u00a311,125k","as_at":"31/03/26","page":8},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a327,335k under-borrowing (budget assumed \u00a336,405k)","as_at":"31/03/2026","page":7},{"name":"investment income","value":"\u00a31.75m internally managed investment income; 4.467% average return on \u00a337m average balance, 34bps over the 90-day SO