ral-fund-and-hra-revenue-outturn-report-2025-2.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"02/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Enc. 3 for General Fund and HRA Revenue Outturn Report (2025/26) and Carry Forward of Budgets","url":"http://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22350/enc-3-for-general-fund-and-hra-revenue-outturn-report-2025-2.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"02/07/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[{"title":"Treasury Management (Q4) Outturn","url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22447/Treasury Management Q4 Outturn.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"2026-07-07","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-05","committee":"Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Budget Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-09","committee":"Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Scrutiny Commission","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Houses of Multiple Occupancy Scrutiny Panel","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Charnwood's rent arrears rise as two-thirds of council tenants fall on to Universal Credit","lead":"Charnwood Borough Council's housing rents arrears have jumped by nearly a fifth in a year, reaching \u00a3650,000 by July, as the council struggles with mounting budget pressures. The increase comes as almost two-thirds of its tenants \u2014 3,186 people \u2014 now rely on Universal Credit, the government's benefit payment system, after the completion of managed migration from older benefits. The average debt of a Universal Credit tenant in arrears has risen to \u00a3466, up from \u00a3419 a year earlier. Meanwhile, the council faces wider financial strain: its reserves for capital spending on long-lived assets like buildings are nearly exhausted, forcing it to borrow for future work, and legal costs are running at four times the annual budget. The council, which is being abolished and succeeded by a new authority, says it needs \"significant savings\" over the rest of the year to protect its housing account's reserves.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"General Fund and HRA Reserves - Cabinet Response","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22977/22977.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Charnwood's housing reserves nearing depletion as council seeks emergency savings","lead":"Charnwood Borough Council's housing account will need to find significant savings over the remainder of the financial year to prevent its capital reserves\u2014money set aside for long-term investment\u2014from depleting further, the Finance and Performance Scrutiny Committee heard this week. The council reported that capital reserves for both its general operations and its housing stock are close to exhaustion following over \u00a330 million already spent on housing improvements. With future capital spending exceeding remaining reserves, virtually all future housing investment will now need to be financed through borrowing, a shift that will increase the council's long-term debt servicing costs. Even the general fund, which runs day-to-day services, will likely require borrowing for its capital plans despite using all available reserves above minimum working balances.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"General Fund and HRA Reserves - Cabinet Response","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22977/22977.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring Report","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22976/22976.pdf","headline":"HRA housing acquisition programme significantly underspent; 24 units delayed to later in year","detail":"HRA capital has spent \u00a33.558m against a profiled budget of \u00a36.905m (52% of profile) at Period 4. The main element, acquisition of affordable housing (\u00a34.2m budget), shows delays with 24 new build units still \"due to complete during the remainder of 2026/27\" rather than spread through the year.","category":"capital","matters":"Housing delivery delays affect capital deployment and revenue implications (rental income timing and debt servicing); 48% underspend at month 4 on a \u00a317.8m programme suggests significant timing slippage.","figures":"HRA full-year budget \u00a317.835m; Period 4 spend \u00a33.558m vs profile \u00a36.905m (52%); housing acquisition budget \u00a34.2m with 24 properties still to complete","quote":"The HRA full-year capital budget is \u00a317.835m, with a Period 4 profiled budget of \u00a36.905m compared with spend and commitments of \u00a33.558m, resulting in an underspend against profile of \u00a33.347m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring Report","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22976/22976.pdf","headline":"Household Food Waste vehicle deliveries delayed by four months; collections now November","detail":"Vehicle production has experienced further delays, pushing delivery from summer to October 2026 and food waste collections from summer to November 2026. The scheme has spent only \u00a313k of its \u00a31.463m budget to date, indicating minimal progress despite the schedule slip.","category":"capital","matters":"Service delivery delays indicate project management risk; the slip affects both capital programme delivery certainty and revenue budget assumptions (collection costs and processing targets now shift).","figures":"Budget \u00a31.463m, Period 4 spend \u00a313k (0.9%); delivery pushed to October, collections to November","quote":"there have been further delays in production of vehicles, and delivery is now expected in October 2026, with food waste collections scheduled for early November 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring Report","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22976/22976.pdf","headline":"Beehive Lane Car Park scheme is overrunning budget and requires \u00a3110k virement","detail":"The scheme has a budget of \u00a3619k but predicted outturn is \u00a3729k, an overspend of \u00a3110k requiring reallocation in the October 2026 Capital Programme Review. By July, the scheme has already spent \u00a3648k (105% of total budget) against a profiled \u00a3178k, indicating substantial cost escalation or scope change.","category":"capital","matters":"A specific scheme actively overrunning budget by 18% signals project management or scope control issues; the scheme has spent its full annual budget by month 4 of 12 with 9 months of delivery remaining.","figures":"Budget \u00a3619k, predicted outturn \u00a3729k (\u00a3110k overspend); Period 4 spend \u00a3648k against budget \u00a3619k","quote":"Beehive Lane Car Park Improvements and Refurbishment Scheme \u2013 the current predicted outturn is \u00a3729k against a current budget of \u00a3619k in 2026/27, and a \u00a3110k virement has been identified for inclusion in the Capital Programme Review going to Cabinet in October 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Capital Monitoring Report","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22976/22976.pdf","headline":"General Fund capital programme is spending 24% faster than quarterly profile","detail":"At Period 4 (July), the General Fund has spent \u00a36.915m against a profiled budget of \u00a35.565m, an overspend of \u00a31.350m (124% of profile). Live schemes are particularly accelerated at 158% of profile (\u00a35.448m actual vs \u00a33.452m profiled). This represents significant pace acceleration four months into the financial year.","category":"capital","matters":"Accelerated capital spending in the first four months suggests either delivery compression or reserve pressure; a lender needs to understand whether this pace is sustainable across the remaining 8 months of the year.","figures":"General Fund Period 4 spend \u00a36.915m vs profiled \u00a35.565m (124%); Live schemes \u00a35.448m vs profiled \u00a33.452m (158%)","quote":"The General Fund full-year capital budget is \u00a324.755m, with a Period 4 profiled budget of \u00a35.565m compared with spend and commitments of \u00a36.915m, resulting in an overspend against profile of \u00a31.350m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Finance & Performance Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Item 9 - 202604 Capital Monitoring Report Master","paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22983/22983.pdf","headline":"\u00a31.46m Household Food Waste Collection vehicle project delayed to October 2026","detail":"The Household Food Waste Caddies and Collection Vehicles capital scheme has experienced further delays, with vehicle delivery now pushed to October 2026 and waste collections starting early November 2026. The reference to 'further delays' indicates multiple postponements.","category":"capital","matters":"Slippage on a \u00a31.46m capital investment may signal procurement or project management challenges, and could delay delivery of planned waste service efficiencies.","figures":"Budget \u00a31,463,000; delivery now October 2026; collections start November 2026","quote":"There have been further delays in production of vehicles and delivery is now expected in October 2026 with collections for food waste scheduled for early November 2026","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Charnwood BC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"HRA housing acquisition programme significantly underspent; 24 units delayed to later in year","lead":"Housing delivery delays affect capital deployment and revenue implications (rental income timing and debt servicing); 48% underspend at month 4 on a \u00a317.8m programme suggests significant timing slippage.","also":["29 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Scrutiny Commission on 2026-10-05","n_findings":30,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Capital Monitoring Report","top_paper_url":"https://charnwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s22976/22976.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":92,"news_drafts_total":2}}